+### task run
+
+Supervise a direct or branch_pr task through its typed lifecycle.
+
+Usage:
+
+```text
+agentplane task run <task-id> [options]
+```
+
+Options:
+
+- `--dry-run`: Prepare runner artifacts and invocation without executing the adapter. (default=false)
+- `--remote`: Include hosted PR/check/review state in the prepared work order. (default=false)
+- `--sandbox <read-only|workspace-write|danger-full-access>`: Override the role-derived sandbox for this run. (choices=read-only|workspace-write|danger-full-access)
+- `--allow-danger-full-access`: Explicitly authorize a requested danger-full-access sandbox and record CLI provenance. (default=false)
+- `--json`: Emit JSON. (default=false)
+
+Notes:
+
+- In direct workflow mode, this command starts an approved task, runs the EXECUTOR, records the observed receipt, and invokes the independent EVALUATOR. It stops with a typed result for approval, missing context, rework, or human review.
+- In branch_pr workflow mode, this command owns safe worktree/start operations, one role-scoped semantic episode, deterministic verification, EVALUATOR review, PR synchronization, integration enqueue, hosted-close, and cleanup. Provider waits and authority requests remain explicit stops.
+- With the default Codex adapter, the runner prompt starts with \`/goal ...\` and then includes the AgentPlane bundle contract.
+
+Examples:
+
+```sh
+agentplane task run 202602030608-F1Q8AB
+```
+
+- Execute the task with the configured runner adapter.
+
+```sh
+agentplane task run 202602030608-F1Q8AB --dry-run --json
+```
+
+- Inspect the prepared runner invocation and artifact paths without starting the agent.
+
